hadiths[81]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2353","[AI-translation] From Zaid bin Harithah, from the Prophet, who said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him at the beginning of what was revealed to him, and taught him wudu and salah. When he finished wudu, he took a handful of water and sprinkled his private parts with it."
"2354","[AI-translation] Walid, Yazid bin Abi Sufyan, Shurahbil bin Hasanh, and Amr bin Al-As, all of these heard from the Messenger of Allah, who said: ""Perfect the wudu; woe to the heels from the Fire."
"2355","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah said: ""When one of you inserts his feet into his leather socks while they are pure, let him wipe over them: three for the traveler, one day and one night for the resident."
"2356","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu': ""When one of you performs istijmar, let him do it an odd number of times, and when one of you sniffs water, let him do it an odd number of times."
"2357","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, who said: ""When one of you awakens from his sleep and performs wudu, let him sniff water up his nose three times, for Satan spends the night on his nostril."
"2358","[AI-translation] From Asma bint Abu Bakr, she said: A woman asked the Messenger of Allah and said: ""What do you think if the blood of menstruation gets on the garment of one of us, what should she do with it?"" The Messenger of Allah said: ""If the blood of menstruation gets on one of you, let her rub it, then wash it with water (and in a narration: then rub it with water, then sprinkle the rest of it), then let her pray in it."
"2359","[AI-translation] From Busrah bint Safwan, that the Prophet said: ""When one of you touches his private part with his hand, let him perform wudu."
"2360","[AI-translation] He said (peace be upon him): When the two circumcised parts meet, the ritual bath has become obligatory. Reported with the wording of ......... and others."
"2361","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When one of you defecates, let him wipe three times. (And in a narration): Let him wipe with three stones. It is reported from the hadith of Jabir, As-Sa'ib bin Khallad, and Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"2362","[AI-translation] Jabir bin Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When two men defecate, let each of them conceal himself from his companion, and let them not converse while they are at their toilet, for Allah detests that."
"2363","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) [said]: When one of you performs ablution and does it well, then goes out to the mosque, nothing diverts him except the prayer, his left foot does not cease to erase a bad deed, and his right foot to write a good deed, until he enters the mosque."
"2364","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: When one of you performs ablution for prayer, let him not interlace his fingers."
"2365","[AI-translation] Ashja'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When you perform ablution, snuffle water, and when you cleanse with stones, use an odd number. (2365) Narrated from Salamah bin Qais Al-Ashja'i (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When you perform ablution, snuffle water, and when you use stones, use an odd number."
"2366","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When you perform ablution, pass water through the fingers of your hands and your feet."
"2367","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, elevated to the Prophet: When one of you sits to relieve himself, let him not face the Qiblah nor turn his back to it."
"2368","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When you circumcise, cut slightly and do not cut deeply, for it is brighter for the face and more favorable to the husband."
"2369","[AI-translation] From Surqah bin Malik bin Ju'sham, that when he came from the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), he would narrate to his people and teach them. A man said to him one day, as if he were mocking: Nothing is left for Surqah except to teach you how to defecate! Surqah said: When you go to the open area to relieve yourselves, avoid places of shade and roads, take your arrows, hold fast to your shins, and cleanse with stones in odd numbers."
"2370","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: That Umm Sulaim asked the Messenger of Allah about a woman who sees in her sleep what a man sees. The Messenger of Allah said: ""If she sees that and experiences discharge, she must perform Ghusl."" Umm Salama said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Can this happen?"" He said: ""Yes. The fluid of a man is thick and white, and the fluid of a woman is thin and yellow. Whichever of the two precedes or dominates, the child will resemble it."
"2371","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah: A man passed by the Prophet while he was urinating and greeted him with Salam. The Messenger of Allah said to him: ""If you see me in such a state, do not greet me with Salam, for if you do that, I will not respond to you."
"2372","[AI-translation] Narrated Aisha from the Prophet: He said: ""If any one of you prays and breaks wind, let him hold his nose and then leave."
"2373","[AI-translation] Juhani: I left Sham for Al-Madinah on Friday, and I entered Al-Madinah on Friday, and I entered upon Umar bin Al-Khattab. He said: ""When did you put your Khuffs on your feet?"" I said: ""On Friday."" He said: ""Did you take them off?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""You have followed the Sunnah."
"2374","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Messenger of Allah said: ""I have frequently enjoined the Siwak upon you."
"2375","[AI-translation] Narrated Safwan bin Umaiyya: A man came to the Messenger of Allah perfumed with Khaluq, wearing patched garments, having entered Ihram for Umrah. He said: ""How do you command me, O Messenger of Allah, regarding my Umrah?"" Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: ""And complete the Hajj and Umrah for Allah"" (Al-Baqarah: 196). The Messenger of Allah said: ""Where is the one asking about Umrah?"" He said: ""Here I am."" He said: ""Take off your garments, perform Ghusl, and sniff water into your nose as much as you can. And whatever you would do in your Hajj, do it in your Umrah."
"2376","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Jurayj: I was informed about Uthaym bin Kulayb (Al-Juhani), from his father, from his grandfather, that he came to the Prophet and said: ""I have embraced Islam."" The Prophet said to him: ""Cast away from you the hair of disbelief,"" meaning, ""Shave."" He said: And another informed me from him that the Prophet said to another: ""Cast away from you the hair of disbelief, and circumcise."
"2377","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas from the Prophet: He said: ""I was commanded to use the Siwak to the extent that I feared for my teeth."
"2378","[AI-translation] Ansari: The Messenger of Allah said: ""Wipe over the Khuffs for three days. And had we sought to increase it, He would have increased it for us."
"2379","[AI-translation] Narrated Hudhayfah: The Messenger of Allah said: ""My Hawd is indeed farther from Aylah to Aden. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, its vessels are more numerous than the stars, and it is whiter than [???] and sweeter than honey. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will drive men away from it just as a man drives away stray camels from his cistern."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, will you recognize us?"" He said: ""Yes, you will come to me with bright and radiant faces and limbs from the traces of Wudu, which will not be for anyone other than you."
"2380","[AI-translation] From Zayd ibn Arqam, elevated to the Prophet: ""Indeed, these toilets are attended. So when one of you goes to the toilet, let him say: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils.'"
"2381","[AI-translation] From 'A'isha, that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said to her regarding menstruation: ""Undo your hair and perform the bath."
"2382","[AI-translation] From 'A'isha, she said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah and said: ""I am a woman who experiences chronic bleeding and does not become pure; should I abandon the prayer?"" He said: ""That is only a vein, and it is not menstruation. So when the menstruation approaches, leave the prayer, and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself (then perform ablution for every prayer until that time arrives) then pray."
"2383","[AI-translation] Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, that he came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, while he was urinating, and he greeted him with salam. He did not return the greeting to him until he had performed ablution. Then he apologized to him, saying: ""I disliked mentioning Allah except in a state of purity,"" or he said, ""in a state of purification."
"2384","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, sent an expedition. They acquired abundant spoils and made a swift return. A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we have never seen an expedition with a swifter return or greater spoils than this one."" He said: ""Shall I not inform you of a swifter return and greater spoils than this? A man performs ablution in his house, perfecting his ablution, then sets out for the mosque and prays the morning prayer, then follows it with the Duha prayer—he has achieved a swifter return and greater spoils."
"2385","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: The two ears are part of the head. Narrated from the hadith of... Abdullah ibn Zayd."
"2386","[AI-translation] From Abu Hazim, he said: I was behind Abu Hurayrah while he was performing ablution for prayer, and he would extend his hand until it reached his armpit. I said to him: ""O Abu Hurayrah, what is this ablution?"" He replied: ""O son of Farrukh! Are you here?! Had I known you were here, I would not have performed this ablution. I heard my beloved say: 'The adornment of a believer reaches where the ablution reaches.'"
"2387","[AI-translation] From Salman, elevated to the Prophet: ""Wipe yourselves with the earth, for it is pure for you."
"2388","On the authority of Abdur-Rahman ibn Jubair ibn Nufair, from his father, that Abu Jubair came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his daughter whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had married. The Prophet ﷺ ordered wudu for him and said: ""Perform wudu, O Abu Jubair."" So Abu Jubair began with his mouth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: ""Do not begin with your mouth, for the disbeliever begins with his mouth."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for the wudu water, washed his hands until he cleansed them, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his right hand up to the elbow three times, and the left three times, wiped his head, and washed his feet."
"2389","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, elevated to the Prophet: ""How excellent are those who use the siwak among my nation."
"2390","[AI-translation] From Umm Qays bint Mihsan, she said: I asked the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said: ""Rub it with a piece of wood and wash it with water and sidr."
"2391","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas who said: A man asked the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, about something concerning prayer, so the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to him: ""Interlace the fingers of your hands and feet,"" meaning the perfection of ablution. And among what he said to him was: ""When you bow, place your palms on your knees until you are tranquil, and when you prostrate, press your forehead to the ground until you feel the firmness of the ground."
"2392","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet, peace be upon him: That he granted a concession to the traveler for three days and their nights, and to the resident for a day and a night — if he purifies himself and puts on his leather socks — to wipe over them."
"2393","[AI-translation] From Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Do right, draw near, act, and give glad tidings, and know that the best of your deeds is the prayer, and none maintains his ablution except a believer."
"2394","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Prayer is three thirds: purification is a third, bowing is a third, and prostration is a third. So whoever fulfills its rights, it is accepted from him, and the rest of his deeds are accepted from him; and whose prayer is rejected, the rest of his deeds are rejected."
"2395","[AI-translation] From Ammar bin Yasir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said regarding Tayammum: ""One strike for the face and the two hands."
"2396","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, elevated to the Prophet: ""A full bath is a Sa', and ablution is a Mudd."
"2397","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar: He, peace be upon him and his family, when he intended to relieve himself, would not raise his garment until he drew near to the ground."
"2398","[AI-translation] From Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, when he came out of the toilet, would perform ablution."
"2399","[AI-translation] Mughirah ibn Shubah, elevated: He, peace be upon him and his family, when he went to relieve himself, would go far away."
"2400","[AI-translation] From Aisha: He, peace be upon him and his family, when the two circumcised parts met, would perform a full bath."
"2401","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah: He (sallallahu alaihi wa aalihi wa sallam), whenever he performed ablution, would run water over his elbows."
"2402","[AI-translation] From Ibrahim, as a mursal report: The Messenger of Allah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) would be known by the scent of perfume when he approached."
"2403","[AI-translation] From 'Urwah: He (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) had a cloth with which he would dry himself after ablution."
"2404","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar: He (sallallahu alaihi wa aalihi wa sallam) would not sleep except with the siwak beside him, and when he woke up, he would begin with the siwak."
"2405","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar who said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Is ablution from a new plastered jug more beloved to you, or from the places of purification (matahir)?"" He said: ""No, rather from the places of purification. Indeed, the religion of Allah is ease; the upright and tolerant faith."" He said: And he would send to the places of purification, and water would be brought, and he would drink it, hoping for the blessing of the hands of the Muslims."
"2406","[AI-translation] From Mahmud bin Tahla' who said: I said to Abu Salamah, ""Your foster-mother Sulaym does not perform ablution from what the fire has touched."" So he struck the chest of Sulaym and said, ""I testify, regarding Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (sallallahu alaihi wa aalihi wa sallam), that she used to testify about the Messenger of Allah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) that he used to perform ablution from what the fire had touched."
"2407","[AI-translation] From Mu'adh bin Jabal: He used to perform ablution one by one, and two by two, and three by three; he would do all of that."
"2408","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas: He (sallallahu alaihi wa aalihi wa sallam) would go out, pour the water, and wipe with the dust. I would say: ""O Messenger of Allah! The water is near you."" He would say: ""And what makes me know? Perhaps I will not reach it."
"2409","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar: He (sallallahu alaihi wa aalihi wa sallam) used to go to al-Mughammis to answer the call of nature. Nafi' said: ""(Al-Mughammis is) two or three miles from Makkah."
"2410","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) said: ""Cleanse the fingertips thoroughly with purification, or the Fire will thoroughly cleanse them."
"2411","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), raising it, he said: Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my Ummah, I would have enjoined upon my Ummah the siwak just as I enjoined upon them wudu."
"2412","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, from Maimuna, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) entered a state of janabah, so I bathed from a large bowl, and some water remained. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) came to bathe from it, so I said, ""I have already bathed from it."" He said: ""There is no janabah upon water."
"2413","[AI-translation] From Khawla bint Hakim, that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) about the woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: ""There is no ghusl upon her until she discharges, just as there is no ghusl upon the man until he discharges."
"2414","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: Salmā, the freed slave woman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—or the wife of Abū Rāfiʿ, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his permission concerning Abū Rāfiʿ, for he had struck her. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abū Rāfiʿ: ""What is between you and her, O Abū Rāfiʿ?"" He said: ""She annoys me, O Messenger of Allah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""How did you annoy him, O Salmā?"" She said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I did not annoy him with anything, but he passed wind while he was praying, so I said to him: 'O Abū Rāfiʿ! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has commanded the Muslims that if wind passes from one of them, he should perform ablution.'"" (And al-Ṭabarānī said: ""That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever passes wind should repeat the ablution.'"") So he stood up and struck me. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to laugh and said: ""O Abū Rāfiʿ! She only ordered you to do good."""
"2415","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, raising it to the Prophet (peace be upon him): Whoever performs istijmar, let him perform it three times."
"2416","[AI-translation] Qasim, the mawla of Mu'awiya, who said: I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw a group of people gathered, and an old man narrating to them. I said: ""Who is this?"" They said: ""Sahl ibn al-Hanzaliyya."" So I heard him saying: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: 'Whoever eats meat, let him perform wudu.'"
"2417","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Whoever spends the night in a state of purity, an angel spends the night in his garment. He does not wake up at any hour of the night except that the angel says: ""O Allah, forgive Your servant so-and-so, for he spent the night in a state of purity."
"2418","[AI-translation] From Salman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs wudu and comes to the mosque, he is a visitor of Allah, and it is a right upon the visited to honor the visitor."
"2419","[AI-translation] From 'A'isha, she said: ""Whoever tells you that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) used to urinate standing, do not believe him. He never urinated except sitting."
"2420","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not face the qibla, nor turns his back to it when relieving himself, a good deed is written for him and a bad deed is erased from him."
"2421","[AI-translation] 'As, that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) passed by Sa'd while he was performing wudu, so he said: ""What is this extravagance, O Sa'd?"" He said: ""Is there extravagance in wudu?"" He said: ""Yes, even if you are upon a flowing river."
"2422","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, called for water for ablution. He washed his face once, his hands once, and his feet once, and said: ""This is an ablution without which Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, does not accept the prayer."" Then he called for water and performed ablution washing twice, and said: ""This is the ablution of whoever performs ablution; Allah will double his reward twice."" Then he called for water and performed ablution washing three times, and said: ""This is the ablution of your Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and of the prophets before him,"" or he said: ""This is my ablution and the ablution of the prophets before me."
"2423","[AI-translation] Narrated Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather (Abdullah ibn Amr): A bedouin came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, asking him about ablution, so he showed him the ablution washing three times each, then said: ""This is the ablution, so whoever exceeds this has done evil, transgressed, and wronged."
"2424","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We ride the sea and carry with us a small amount of water. If we perform ablution with it, we will suffer from thirst. Should we perform ablution with it?"" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Its water is pure, and its dead are lawful."
"2425","[AI-translation] Narrated Aisha: She made a jubbah of black wool for the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family. He put it on, but when he sweated, he noticed the smell of the wool, so he took it off. He used to like a pleasant scent."
"2426","[AI-translation] Narrated Umm Salamah: She said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I am a woman who tightly braids my hair; should I undo it for the ritual bath of major impurity?"" He said: ""No, it is only sufficient for you to pour three handfuls on your head, then pour water over yourself and you will be purified."
"2427","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was asked, and it was said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who commits hadath, performs ablution, and wipes over his khuffs, can he pray?"" He said: ""There is no harm in that."
"2428","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Uqaym: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Do not derive benefit from the dead animal, neither its tanned hide nor its sinew."
"2429","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Yazid, from the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""Urine should not be left to soak in a basin in the house, for the angels do not enter a house in which there is urine, and do not urinate in a bathing place."
"2430","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""A mudd is sufficient for ablution, and a sa' for the ritual bath."" It is narrated from the hadith of Aqil... and Abdullah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them."
"2431","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: Abu Dharr was with a small flock of his at Al-Rabadhah. When he came, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said to him: ""O Abu Dharr!"" but he remained silent. He repeated it, and he remained silent. Then he said: ""O Abu Dharr! May your mother lose you!"" He replied: ""I am in a state of major ritual impurity."" So he called the slave girl for water, and she brought it to him. He shielded himself with his mount and performed the ritual bath, then came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said to him: ""The clean earth is sufficient for you, even if you do not find water for twenty years (and in a narration: ten years), but when you find it, touch it to your skin."
"2432","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, marfu'an: The one who spits toward the Qibla will come on the Day of Resurrection and it will be on his face."
"2433","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah that Khawla bint Yasar came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have only one garment, and I menstruate in it, so what should I do? He said: When you become pure, wash it, then pray in it. She said: What if the blood does not come out? He said: The water is sufficient for you, and its trace will not harm you."
